<title>NETHERLANDS: OCE IN TALKS TO BUY SIEMENS' LEASE PORTFOLIO.</title>
<headline>OCE IN TALKS TO BUY SIEMENS' LEASE PORTFOLIO.</headline>
<dateline>VENLO, Netherlands 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch photocopier maker Oce NV said on Thursday it was in talks with U.S. Siemens Credit Corporation on acquiring a lease contract portfolio for printers placed in the market by Siemens Nixdorf Informationssysteme (SNI) in the past.</p>
<p>In 1996, Oce bought the printing activities of SNI, but the lease portfolio for printers was left out of the deal.</p>
<p>Oce said it aimed to complete the deal at 31 July, 1997 at the latest. No financial details of the deal were disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
